{"questions":[{"question_id":"1l31cmcip","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2010 Paper 1 Offline","year":2010,"examDate":2010,"subject":"physics","chapter":"current-electricity","chapterGroup":"electricity","topic":"ohms-law","type":"mcq","marks":3,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"pto-verify-ohms-law-a-student-is-provided-with-a-test-re-jee-advanced-physics-current-electricity-lgf7edkir2d0xuxs","content":"<p>To verify Ohm's law, a student is provided with a test resitor R<sub>T</sub>, a high resistance R<sub>1</sub>, a small resistance R<sub>2</sub>, two identical galvanometers G<sub>1</sub> and G<sub>2</sub>, and a variable voltage source V. The correct circuit to carry out the experiment is</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"<img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l31snx1d/96b57a4a-9da7-4916-b2d1-4f4ca3cd3793/257dd710-d147-11ec-8987-f18bea11de09/file-1l31snx1e.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l31snx1d/96b57a4a-9da7-4916-b2d1-4f4ca3cd3793/257dd710-d147-11ec-8987-f18bea11de09/file-1l31snx1e.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2010 Paper 1 Offline Physics - Current Electricity Question 14 English Option 1\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l31snx1d/96b57a4a-9da7-4916-b2d1-4f4ca3cd3793/257dd710-d147-11ec-8987-f18bea11de09/file-1l31snx1e.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l31snx1d/96b57a4a-9da7-4916-b2d1-4f4ca3cd3793/257dd710-d147-11ec-8987-f18bea11de09/file-1l31snx1e.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l31snx1d/96b57a4a-9da7-4916-b2d1-4f4ca3cd3793/257dd710-d147-11ec-8987-f18bea11de09/file-1l31snx1e.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l31snx1d/96b57a4a-9da7-4916-b2d1-4f4ca3cd3793/257dd710-d147-11ec-8987-f18bea11de09/file-1l31snx1e.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly